- START is **per-stream, not per-buffer**: `wm8994_start` (wm8994.c:1255-1329) only creates the worker mq `/tmp/%p` and spawns the worker thread "wm8994" at `SCHED_FIFO max-3`. Buffers stream through the worker (`wm8994_workerthread` :1747+, mq loop, calls `wm8994_sendbuffer` :1170-1252 which keeps up to `CONFIG_WM8994_INFLIGHT` transfers outstanding via `I2S_SEND(priv-&gt;i2s, apb, wm8994_senddone, priv, timeout)` :1241, with the timeout computed from buffer size/rate :1234-1242). Completion: `wm8994_returnbuffers` (:1103-1158) returns each done buffer via `priv-&gt;dev.upper(..., AUDIO_CALLBACK_DEQUEUE, apb, OK)`; the buffer carrying `AUDIO_APB_FINAL` sets `priv-&gt;terminating = true` (:1126-1141) and the worker ends with `AUDIO_CALLBACK_COMPLETE` (worker tail, wm8994.c:~1905-1918).
- SAI buffer constraints (`sai_send`, stm32_sai.c:1519+): rejects `apb-&gt;nbytes &gt; apb-&gt;nmaxbytes` or `curbyte &gt; nbytes` (-EINVAL :1531-1534); requires `bytes % unit == 0` and `addr % unit == 0` where `unit = datalen &gt; 16 ? 4 : 2` (:1536-1543, i.e. 2-byte or 4-byte alignment); rejects `bytes/unit &gt; DMA_SNDTR_NDT_MASK` (-E2BIG, 16-bit NDTR, so max 65535 units ≈ 128/256 KB per transfer — 8192 is fine); rejects buffers straddling the DTCM boundary (-EFAULT :1547-1550). DMA is single-beat MINC with PSIZE/MSIZE matched to the data width (stm32_sai.c:117-161); playback is not circular (circular mode exists for capture, :300, :2273).

