## 6. Poll support — yes

The audio char dev registers a poll method: `audio_poll` in `g_audioops` (nuttx/audio/audio.c:148, implementation :1373-1413). On setup it immediately notifies `POLLIN | POLLOUT` (plus `POLLERR` when `(long)(priv-&gt;head - upper-&gt;status-&gt;tail) &lt;= 0`) if `priv-&gt;head - upper-&gt;status-&gt;tail != upper-&gt;periods` (audio.c:1391-1400), i.e. readable/writable when the internal ring has a free slot. Each completed buffer wakes pollers from `audio_dequeuebuffer` (audio.c:1506-1518). Note this poll readiness is defined for the *internal-ring* (u.buffer == NULL) mode; a user-buffer player still only learns of completion through its registered mqueue or by polling `AUDIOIOC_GETSTATUS` for `head`/`tail` advances.

### Minimal-ioctl sequence implied by the above (for reference)
open `/dev/audio/pcm0p` → `AUDIOIOC_GETCAPS`(OUTPUT/QUERY) → `AUDIOIOC_RESERVE` → `AUDIOIOC_CONFIGURE`(caps_desc: OUTPUT, channels, chmap, rate in `ac_controls.hw[0] | b[3]&lt;&lt;16`, bpsamp in `b[2]`, subtype `AUDIO_FMT_PCM`) → `AUDIOIOC_GETBUFFERINFO` (expect 8192 × 4) → `AUDIOIOC_ALLOCBUFFER` ×4 → mq_open + `AUDIOIOC_REGISTERMQ` → fill + `AUDIOIOC_ENQUEUEBUFFER` ×4 → `AUDIOIOC_START` → loop on `mq_receive` (`AUDIO_MSG_DEQUEUE` → refill/re-enqueue; `AUDIO_MSG_COMPLETE` → done; last buffer gets `AUDIO_APB_FINAL`) → `AUDIOIOC_FREEBUFFER` ×4, `AUDIOIOC_UNREGISTERMQ`, `AUDIOIOC_RELEASE`, close. There is no blocking enqueue, no AUDIOIOC_SETUP, no AUDIOIOC_ABORT.</result>
